# Level 4-03: Catch the Platform — a single tightly-timed live loop (no ghost needed at all):
# ride a MovingPlatform across a one-tile chasm the instant it arrives, then clear a box that
# blocks the only route onward with a single sideways push. One-tile-wide spine at x=3 from
# spawn (3,0) up through the platform's near waypoint P (3,2); the chasm itself (y=3) is plain
# wall — MovingPlatform.WaypointAt jumps the platform directly between its two named waypoint
# coordinates every tick, with no interpolation through the tiles between, so the far waypoint Q
# (3,4) needs no walkable path of its own back to spawn, only the ride. (This is the one
# deliberate exception to "every floor tile reachable by walking back to spawn" the brief allows
# for platform/teleport levels — hand-verified here via the trace below, exactly as the brief
# requires.) From Q the path bends: at (3,5) the live player pushes a box one tile sideways from
# (4,5) into the dead-end alcove at (5,5), stands on the now-clear tile, then continues to the
# goal at (4,7). Every tile — including the alcove — is a plain dead end off this single path.
#
# ticksPerStep=2 is chosen so the platform's first A->B jump lands on exactly the tick the
# player's own walk reaches waypoint A — zero wasted waiting.
#
# Loop 0 (only loop — no ghost is ever created; PAR_LOOPS is the true minimum of 1):
#   t0 Up (3,0)->(3,1). t1 Up (3,1)->(3,2)=P (waypoint A, order 0). Position-before-tick check
#     for the platform: WaypointAt(0)=WaypointAt(1)=A (since floor(0/2)=floor(1/2)=0), so the
#     platform has been sitting at A this whole time and the player's walk-on is unaffected by it.
#   t2 Idle (must not move away from P this tick to stay eligible for the carry): WaypointAt(2)
#     = waypoints[(2/2)%2] = waypoints[1] = Q — the platform's pre-tick position (A, carried over
#     from t1) differs from its post-tick position (Q), so GridWorld.Step's carry rule relocates
#     any actor still sitting at A to Q. The player, having idled, is carried: (3,2)->(3,4).
#     (Choosing ticksPerStep=2 means this is the earliest possible tick a ride is available at
#     all — the player loses zero ticks beyond the 2 needed just to walk there.)
#   t3 Up (3,4)->(3,5).
#   t4 Right (3,5)->(4,5): a box sits at (4,5) with the alcove (5,5) empty behind it, so the push
#     succeeds in the same tick as the move — box (4,5)->(5,5), player -> (4,5).
#   t5 Up (4,5)->(4,6).
#   t6 Up (4,6)->(4,7)=goal. WinCondition satisfied at tick 6.
# Totals: 1 loop used (no ghost recording ever needed) -> PAR_LOOPS: 1.
#   7 ticks executed (indices 0-6) -> PAR_TICKS: 6 (exact — every tick above is either a forced
#   single-tile move, the one mandatory idle-for-the-carry tick, or the combined push tick; none
#   can be skipped or merged).
#   7 ticks / 12 = 0.583s, +~1.4s buffer -> LOOP_SECONDS: 2 (also comfortably covers a player's
#   reaction time getting onto the platform before its first, only relevant, transition at t2).
NAME: 4-03 Catch the Platform
WORLD: 4
LOOP_SECONDS: 2
MAX_TIMELINES: 1
PAR_LOOPS: 1
PAR_TICKS: 6
GRID:
####G####
####.####
###.X.###
###Q#####
#########
###P#####
###.#####
###S#####
LEGEND:
S=spawn G=goal X=box P=platform:plat1:0:2 Q=platform:plat1:1:2
